WEBVTT

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.040
So,

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.950
I'd like to hear your report, Girghe.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:25.140
I did step aside amidst the chaos
and once I regained myself, wandered about.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.880
During which, found myself under enemy fire and fled.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:28.550
That is all.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.210
That's not what I heard from Rygart.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:37.380
You destroyed seven Golems, partially destroyed
two officer's units and nearly crippled another.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.190
...Oh, right, I did that too.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:48.590
Girghe, you are hereby forbidden to carry a firearm
or approach a Golem without my explicit approval.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:55.120
Captain Narvi, may Girghe be allowed
to oversee the repairs to his Artemis?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.030
Come with me, Girghe!

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.680
Yes, ma'am.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.270
What's with that guy?

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.110
Mr. Loggin, I have an important message.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:14.370
About a year ago, I was on my way home
from patrolling the border when it happened.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.380
Girghe had already been imprisoned.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.890
I went to his cell in hopes that I could learn why he did it,

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:29.700
but he would only stare into space
or sneer at me. He refused to speak.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:38.730
Girghe was using one of ten
Golems during a routine marching exercise.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:44.150
Suddenly, he fired on a
comrade and used him as a shield.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:53.330
He then dispatched the remaining eight Golems
without receiving so much as a scratch on his own.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:00.720
After that, he turned himself in.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.540
That's the gist of it.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:09.380
But is that what really happened?

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.860
I mean, he was the only one who lived, right?

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.340
No. Only the first victim died.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.480
He avoided the remaining eight's vitals.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:28.280
Girghe never had any grudges
or rivalries with those other men.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.100
There are several weapons before you.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.200
Pick whichever you like.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.890
Very impressive.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.850
What!? General True is dead!?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.390
What about his remains?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.280
The enemy took possession of them.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:54.330
Speaking of which, Nile...

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:58.460
How do you intend to tell Captain Narvi?

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.560
The decision is yours.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:06.120
She loved the man like a father.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:10.900
Can you guarantee she won't become a
hindrance to future operations upon hearing this?

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.060
I'm afraid not, sir.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.280
Being a hindrance would be the least of our worries.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:23.440
I see. So we're left with two choices.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.970
Either Loggin takes over as captain,

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:30.750
or we keep her in the dark.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:42.410
We were soundly defeated.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.280
Indeed. It was a disgrace.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.310
I even allowed Sir Iris to die.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.250
What?

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.160
I'll make them pay...

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:59.580
Were it not for Colonel Io's assistance,
the General would have been in grave danger.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:03.870
I will slaughter every last Krishnan pig...

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:10.510
That concludes my report on the
Krisnan Artemis and the Black Golem.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:13.080
Leto, what's our current situation?

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:13.970
Sir.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:19.150
Our right wing retreated along a separate route, but were annihilated by General Baldr's forces.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:24.520
Of our forces that fought in the
Arracan wastes, only 60% remain.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.150
However, we still managed to
rendezvous with the main force.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:32.540
Correct. Our force now numbers 120 strong.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.280
So in short, we may consider this skirmish a draw?

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.950
The Krisnans are not to be taken lightly.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.890
And what of the General?

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:45.620
He's chosen to spend the night in the Hicherion.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:53.070
Sorry, Iris...

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.000
I just can't contain my excitement.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:02.730
Especially with those two enemy Golems running around.

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:11.220
Girghe, we're pulling out.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.380
You have permission to approach your Artemis.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.040
But you're not to board it until I give the order!

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.970
Roger that, Captain.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.010
Very well!

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.160
Where's General Baldr?

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:30.750
What's the matter?

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.870
Borcuse is on the move.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.530
He's headed towards Pegusa.

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:35.560
Pegusa?!

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.690
Are you sure?

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.990
We've confirmed that he's taking a detour there.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:41.100
This way.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.830
Rygart.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:45.280
Wait a second! There's a tiny village near Pegusa.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:48.910
Have the residents been evacuated yet?

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:55.140
If they don't make it in time, will Borcuse attack?

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.560
Why, is there something about that village?

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:02.560
That village near Pegusa... is my hometown.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.250
My little brother, Regarz, lives on the outskirts.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.400
What?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.130
I see. Inform General Baldr at once.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.700
Rygart, I'm sure they'll inform the villagers.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.130
Right now, we need to get moving.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.660
Rygart! Pack it in!

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:23.050
Right...

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:25.800
Wait! Stop right there!

00:08:36.200 --> 00:09:03.120
Rygart!

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:16.250
Regarz...

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.940
And here I thought I'd just swing by town...

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.560
What are you doing here?

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.560
Borcuse.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.250
Please step aside, sir!

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.340
Hold your fire!

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:41.670
Nobody is to move a muscle!

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.900
Anyone who interferes will be executed.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:20.990
What a peculiar stance.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:48.860
Those are some clever moves!

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:51.620
But you're wide open when you come down!

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:21.100
When it comes to jointed weapons,
I have a bit of an edge!

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:21.800
What!?

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.530
What's wrong? I'm wide open.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.450
If you're going to kill me, now's your chance.

00:12:56.520 --> 00:13:00.270
Tell me, why did you come to this backwater village alone?

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.390
Something tells me you aren't lost.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.710
What went through your mind when you saw the villagers?

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:11.300
Did you think, "That's just a part of war"?

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:16.760
There must be some reason you've come here alone.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.240
But you were just too late.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:23.520
What will you do?

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:37.730
<i>He's trying to grab my arm!</i>

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.910
General!

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.510
W-Where the hell is Bardess?

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:17.870
It was a smart move to let my Hicherion go airborne.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:25.840
If I had tried to stand my ground and guard, the frame would've given way from that hit.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:45.930
<i>All I've got left is the Eastern Blade.</i>

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:51.090
Now what? Are you going to fly off?

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:54.990
I still can't figure out why you came here by yourself.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.560
But that makes this little detour worth it.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:02.960
Those maneuvers can't be done with quartz ligaments.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.600
A relic from ages past, I suspect.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:10.130
That might be just the thing Orlando needs!

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:12.860
What a fortunate find!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.230
Charging right at your opponent...

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:11.420
You bore me.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:15.190
You can't even close the gap between us.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:19.760
You've gone and ruined my good mood.

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:22.650
Tie him down.

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:28.270
Chains won't cut it! I want five
Golems holding him down too!

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:31.680
I want to transport it home with minimal damage.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:35.840
Tear open the cockpit and drag the pilot out.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.580
Then kill him.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:43.000
Sir, how many times have I told
you not to charge into battle alone?

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:48.740
I couldn't accurately determine the Black Golem's
combat prowess unless I fought him myself.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:52.240
But once I did, it became painfully clear.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:55.710
It's not the pilot that makes that Golem so powerful.

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:59.480
That wasn't the fighting style of a soldier.

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:03.900
My interest is now held by that man in the Artemis.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:11.010
We were too late.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:17.680
40 units headed southwest,
but there's still about 20 left.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:19.940
Plus about 200 infantry.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:25.440
It's just a matter of time
until they yank him out of there.

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:45.620
Umm, Sigyn...

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:48.750
Could you continue your story from yesterday?

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:50.890
Which one?

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:55.460
I was talking about the one where Rygart and
Hodr tried to sneak into the girl's dormitories,

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:58.090
and Zess had to rescue them.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.490
Oh yes.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:03.700
The security at the academy was quite strict.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.570
The girl's dorms in particular. No boys were allowed.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:13.000
No less than eight female guards were stationed around the clock.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:22.080
There was also a rumor that a boy had been
shot dead ages ago trying to sneak inside.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.500
They were so fired up.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:29.620
So did Zess save them from being shot?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.920
Supposedly, they invited him along...

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:35.370
That's ridiculous. I hope you get shot.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:38.810
So did they make it inside?

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:41.620
That night, I heard shots from a Pressure Gun.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:45.860
I looked out my window and
saw two silhouettes running away.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:49.060
They were chased off, like I expected.

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:53.570
Eventually, Zess came to their rescue, and they got away safely.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:19:00.230
That's worlds apart from the Zess I know.

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:08.170
Zess was never one to show emotion
to myself or others. He was very mature.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.680
But whenever he was around Hodr and Rygart,
he turned into a child again.

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:20.580
Especially around Rygart. They fought all the time...

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:35.750
Dammit!

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:41.420
The pilot's regained consciousness!

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:42.230
Pin him down!

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:45.060
They're restraining me!

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:53.510
Loggin, open fire!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:54.780
Come on!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:19:59.630
No good!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.550
It doesn't matter! Keep shooting!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:04.040
Enemy attack! Take cover!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.630
Look at me, Rygart!

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:19.720
Jump!

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:29.580
Sorry, Narvi!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.530
Shut it, idiot!

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.950
Retreat!

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:40.740
The next time you ignore my
orders will be your last, got it!?

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:45.080
Did you find your brother?

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:49.020
So all you did was drag your
comrades into your own mess?

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:51.200
Let's go. They're right behind us.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:51.730
Right.

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:55.450
The enemy?

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:56.360
Take cover!

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.290
Did they catch up already?!

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:04.420
No, it's too soon. Must be another squad.

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:10.530
Girghe, what the hell are you doing?!

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:12.810
Don't expose yourself!

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:14.620
Loggin!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:21.670
You're mine!

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:24.100
Nile, get behind her!

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:25.350
Narvi!

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:38.200
You little shit!

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:45.600
Don't even try it!

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:50.520
What's your problem, Girghe!?

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:53.460
Let's go back! I'm worried about the others!

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:56.380
Worried? Now there's a surprise.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:02.700
Not something I'd expect from a
guy who just ran off on his own.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:07.280
Besides, you got us into this mess.

00:22:07.280 --> 00:22:11.110
That's why we need to go back right now!

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:12.160
Pathetic.

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:15.060
You couldn't even find your brother.

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:18.250
Girghe...

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:53.670
Quit talking as if you're some sort of big shot.

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:55.400
You're just being naive.

00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:59.020
Lightning speed, Godspeed Muso.
